as -- Command

Z8001 assembler
as [-glx] [-o outfile] file ...

as assembles Z8001 assembly language into a relocatable l.out object, which
ld links with other objects and with libraries produced by ar.  It is the
assembler cc runs over the code generator's output: the driver execs it by
the name `as' off its command path.

Every file named on the command line is assembled, in the order given, into
ONE object file.  With no file named, as prints its usage message and exits
non-zero.  Options and file names may be interspersed.

Options
-g     Make global every symbol that is referenced and never defined, as
       though each had been named in a .globl directive.
-l     Write a listing -- error flags, address, generated code, line number
       and source line -- to the standard output.
-o outfile
       Write the object to outfile.  The default is l.out.
-x     Leave local compiler-generated symbols out of the object's symbol
       table: a symbol is written only if it is global or its name does not
       begin with `L'.

Any other option is refused with the usage message

     Usage: as [-glx] [-o file] file [file ...]

The Machine
The assembler this system builds is the segmented one: SEGCPU is 1 in
src/as/z8001/asmch.h, so its CPU is the Zilog Z-8001.  One assembler
produces both forms, and a source file chooses with the .seg and .nonseg
directives.

Register names are the Zilog ones: the words r0 through r15, the byte
halves rh0 through rh7 and rl0 through rl7, the register pairs rr0, rr2,
rr4, rr6, rr8, rr10, rr12 and rr14, and the quadruples rq0, rq4, rq8 and
rq12.

Directives
.          The location counter.
.byte .word .long
           Emit initialised data: one byte, one word or one long per
           expression.
.ascii     Emit a string.
.blkb .blkw .blkl
           Reserve uninitialised space, counted in bytes, words or longs.
.comm      Declare a common block.
.globl     Make a symbol global.
.even .odd Align the location counter.
.seg .nonseg
           Assemble for the segmented (Z8001) or the non-segmented (Z8002)
           form.
.page .title
           Listing control.

Diagnostics
as counts the errors it detects and exits non-zero if the count is not
zero.  The count itself is printed, as `<n> errors detected.', only when a
listing was asked for with -l.

Files
l.out      the object file, when -o names none

